              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A front was a major military formation. Appearing to originate with the Russian Empire, it has been used by the Polish Army, the Red Army and Soviet Army, and by Turkey. It was roughly equivalent to an army group in the militaries of most other countries. It should not to be confused with the more general usage of military front, describing a geographic area in wartime."@en;
