                       <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chief_Marshal>;
                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """The ranks of Marshal of a branch and Chief Marshal of a branch were senior military ranks of the Soviet Armed Forces. Immediately above the rank \"Marshal of a branch\" is the rank \"Chief Marshal of a branch\". Both ranks are immediately above the rank \"Colonel General\" and equal to Soviet General of the Army. The ranks were created as an analog to Air Marshal and Air Chief Marshal, though they weren't used just in the Soviet Air Force but also in the several Soviet Army's branch commands."""@en;
                       <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Chief Marshal".
