                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Chiliarch>;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Chiliarch, in the Greek army of the Hellenistic period, was a commander of a 1,000 men unit, roughly equivalent to a modern battalion. The office was an adaptation by Alexander the Great of the Persian Achaemenid empire's hazarapatish. A chiliarch heldl duties both martial and civil. Alexander the Great first awarded this rank to Hephaestion Amyntoros, but after Hephaestion's death it was awarded to Perdiccas."@en;
                   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Chiliarch".
