                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Colonel>;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Colonel, abbreviated as Col or COL, is a military rank of a senior commissioned officer. It or a corresponding rank exists in most armies and in many air forces; the naval equivalent rank is generally \"Captain\". It is also used in some police forces and other paramilitary rank structures. A colonel is typically in charge of a regiment in an army. \"Colonel\" is usually the highest or second-highest field rank, and is below the general ranks."""@en;
