mil:Rank_Corporal_EnglishTradition mil:rankOf mil:EnglishTradition;
                                   <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#inDataset> mil:datasetdefinition;
                                   a mil:MilitaryRank,
                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>;
                                   rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                                   rdfs:label "Caporal"@fr,
                                              "Korporal"@de,
                                              "Corporal"@en;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Corporal>;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Corporal is a rank in use in some form by most militaries and by some police forces or other uniformed organizations. It is usually equivalent to NATO Rank Code OR-4. The rank of corporal nominally corresponds to commanding a section or squad of soldiers. However, in the United States Army, but not the U.S. Marines, a corporal is usually a fire team leader or second-in-command of a squad of soldiers."@en;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> mil:ArmyServiceBranch,
                                                                                  mil:AirForceServiceBranch;
