                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Divisional General is a rank used in many armies to denote a rank of general, corresponding to command of a division. For convenience Divisional General is almost always translated into English as Major-General, the equivalent rank used by the UK, USA, etc. , although this translation is, strictly speaking, incorrect. The rank is particularly common in western Europe and Latin America."@en;
