mil:Rank_Ferik <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#inDataset> mil:datasetdefinition;
               a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
                 mil:MilitaryRank;
               rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
               rdfs:label "Ferik (rank)"@en;
               <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Ferik_%28rank%29>;
               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Ferik was a military rank of the Ottoman Army. It is translated as Major General or Lieutenant General (Korgeneral). It was superior to a Mirliva (\"Brigadier\") and junior to a Birinci Ferik (\"First Ferik/General\"). The title of Ferik was abolished with Act No. 2590 of 26 November 1934 on the Abolition of Titles and Appellations such as Efendi, Bey or Pasha."""@en;
               <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Ferik".
