                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Gefreiter>;
                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Gefreiter is the German, Swiss and Austrian equivalent for the military rank Private (NATO Rank Code OR-2). Gefreiter was the lowest rank to which an ordinary soldier could be promoted. As a military rank it has existed since at least the 16th century. From the 1920s on Gefreiter has expanded into several additional ranks, those being Obergefreiter, Hauptgefreiter, Stabsgefreiter and Oberstabsgefreiter (NATO Rank Code OR-3 and OR-4). Gefreiter means \"the exempted\"."""@en;
                   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Gefreiter".
