                <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Hetman>;
                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Hetman was the title of the second-highest military commander in 15th- to 18th-century Poland and the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, which together, from 1569 to 1795, comprised the Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, or Rzeczpospolita. \"Hetman\" was also the highest military office, and head of state, in Ukraine's Cossack Hetmanate. The title (Ð³ÐµÑÑÐ¼Ð°Ð½) was used by Ukraine's Cossacks from the 16th century, and by the Czechs (hejtman) in Bohemia from the Hussite Wars (15th century) on."""@en;
                <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Hetman".
