mil:Rank_Lord_High_Admiral_of_the_Wash <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#inDataset> mil:datasetdefinition;
                                       a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
                                         mil:MilitaryRank;
                                       rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                                       rdfs:label "Lord High Admiral of the Wash"@en;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Lord_High_Admiral_of_the_Wash>;
                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The position of Lord High Admiral of the Wash is an ancient hereditary naval office of England. In mediaeval times, the Lord High Admiral of the Wash was a nobleman with responsibility for the defence and protection of The Wash coast in north East Anglia. The post was granted to the le Strange family after the Norman Conquest. In the 16th century the post became obsolete and the Royal Navy took over the defence of the area."@en;
                                       <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Lord High Admiral of the Wash".
