                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """A polemarch was a senior military title in various ancient Greek city states (poleis). The title is composed out of the polemos (war) and archon (ruler/leader) and translates as \"warleader\" or \"warlord\", one of the nine archontes (á¼ÏÏÎ¿Î½ÏÎµÏ) appointed annually in Athens. The name indicates that the polemarchos original function was to command the army; presumably the office was created to take over this function from the king."""@en;
                   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Polemarch".
