                        mil:MilitaryRank;
                      rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                      rdfs:label "Rear admiral"@en;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Rear_admiral>;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Rear admiral is a naval commissioned officer rank above that of a commodore and captain, and below that of a vice admiral. It is generally regarded as the lowest of the \"admiral\" ranks, which are also sometimes referred to as \"flag officers\" or \"flag ranks\". In many navies it is referred to as a two-star rank. It originated from the days of naval sailing squadrons and can trace its origins to the Royal Navy."""@en;
                      <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Rear admiral".
