mil:Rank_Trooper <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#inDataset> mil:datasetdefinition;
                 a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
                   mil:MilitaryRank;
                 rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                 rdfs:label "Trooper (rank)"@en;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Trooper_%28rank%29>;
                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> """Trooper (abbr. Tpr) from the French \"troupier\" is the equivalent rank to private in a regiment with a cavalry tradition in the British Army and many other Commonwealth armies, including those of Australia, Canada, South Africa and New Zealand. Today, most cavalry units operate in the armoured role, equipped with tanks or other armoured fighting vehicles. Some armoured regiments without a cavalry tradition do not use the rank, although the British Royal Tank Regiment does."""@en;
                 <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Trooper".
