                                   rdfs:label "Vice-Admiral of the Coast"@en;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vice-Admiral_of_the_Coast>;
                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The holder of the post Vice-Admiral of the Coast was responsible for the defence of one of the twenty maritime counties of England, the North and South of Wales, or the four provinces of Ireland. As a Vice-Admiral, the post holder was the chief of naval administration for his district. His responsibilities included pressing men for naval service, deciding the lawfulness of prizes (captured by pirate ships), dealing with salvage claims for wrecks and acting as a judge."@en;
                                   <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Vice-Admiral of the Coast".
