mil:Rank_Vice-Admiral_of_the_West <http://rdfs.org/ns/void#inDataset> mil:datasetdefinition;
                                  a <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept>,
                                    mil:MilitaryRank;
                                  rdfs:isDefinedBy <http://rdf.muninn-project.org/ontologies/military>;
                                  rdfs:label "Vice-Admiral of the West"@en;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Vice-Admiral_of_the_West>;
                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The historical title Vice-Admiral of the West is sometimes applied to holders of the crown appointment Vice-Admiral of the Coast of counties in the South West of England. The duties of a Vice-Admiral of the coast were to control the shipping (especially piracy) around a maritime county's coast and organise defense on land and at sea. He also acted as a local judge to deal with maritime matters."@en;
                                  <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Vice-Admiral of the West".
