                                 "Wachmistrz"@pl,
                                 "ÐÐ°ÑÐ¼Ð¸ÑÑÑ"@ru;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs> <http://dbpedia.org/resource/Wachtmeister>;
                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Wachtmeister (German for master-sentinel; watch-master) was a German, Austrian and Swiss military rank of non-commissioned officers. It was also adopted into Russian Army vakhmistr and was used as Sergeant-grade rank in cavalry (until 1826), then Special Corps of Gendarmes and Cossack cavalry and Cossack Leib Guard units. Also, the Polish army used the rank Wachmistrz as a cavalry-specific title for Sergeant. This was similar to calling cavalry Captains Rittmeister."@en;
                      <http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/name> "Wachtmeister".
